2940 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502938 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502938 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the antiderivative of $\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}?$ Assume $x>0$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502938 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "aa70fb16-17a5-5816-9e73-90243c9b4ed6" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502938 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}={x}^{-6}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-6$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{6}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-6+1}}{-6+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{{x}^{-5}}{5}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{5{x}^{5}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502948 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502899 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502948 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502948 #edb/ref 1071 "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[6]{{x}^{7}}}$. Assume $x>0$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502948 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cc7d7a47-ab4b-5a3b-8ff4-ed432aa440ba" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502948 #edb/ref 1074 "Note that $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[6]{{x}^{7}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{7/6}}={x}^{-7/6}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{7}{6}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[6]{{x}^{7}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-7/6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-7/6+1}}{-\\frac{7}{6}+1}+C \\\\  & =-6{x}^{-1/6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{{x}^{1/6}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502954 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186502918 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502954 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502954 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{9/5}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502954 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "de2aa536-e15f-5af4-b511-e0e4c9d378a1" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186502954 #edb/ref 1074 "Remember that integration is the opposite of differen